# Date input

Use separate day, month and year fields for a date the user already knows.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it to record a known filter replacement date or the date an installation was completed. Keep the units visible and accept leading zeros without making people retype them.

## When not to use it

Do not use these three fields to choose an Energy reporting range or find an available date. Preserve Home Assistant’s native date-range controls for exploration.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Group the fields as one question and validate the whole calendar date, including leap years. A date-only maintenance record is not a timestamp: do not silently shift it when the account timezone changes. Do not use birthday autocomplete attributes for appliance dates.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Give every part its own label and numeric input mode, then associate the group hint and error. Link an error summary to the first incorrect part. Keep correct parts intact after a failed submission.

