## Check the implementation

Test missing parts,31 February, an unexpected future date and mobile number keyboards. Explain any domain-specific date restriction in plain language rather than rejecting it as “invalid”.

Use the [civica.uk accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS date input](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/date-input) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica.uk markup, Arial typography and civica.uk assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

